    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0286" n="276" xml:id="pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/1463: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-29T00:00:00+01:00">March 29,
                            1943—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received March 30—12:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>758. I delivered the following note to the Foreign Minister this morning: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of the Ministry’s <hi
                                rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> number 182 of March 25, 1943
                            stating that the Spanish Government has ordered the complete closing of
                            the Pyrenees frontier to those persons not in possession of legal
                            documentation. I have transmitted the contents of this note to my
                                Government.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d259-f1"/>
                        </p>
                        <p>This Embassy has been assured by the Foreign Office on a number of
                            occasions that the Spanish Government would not return refugees of
                            belligerent or occupied countries to the countries of their origin or to
                            territory occupied by the enemy without their consent. I should like to
                            be able to inform my Government promptly that this policy of the Spanish
                            Government has not been modified in any degree.</p>
                        <p>I avail myself of this occasion to renew to Your Excellency the
                            assurances of my highest consideration.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>My 734, March 27, 11 a.m. repeated to Algiers for Murphy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d259-f1" n="33" xml:id="d259-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted in the Ambassador’s telegram No. 734, March 27, 11 a.m., not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
